Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Topological order in install-from-source.txt is split into
    Tier A through Tier J with comment delimiters; each tier's
    components have no inter-tier-skip deps so pip's resolver
    walk is monotonic.
  - install-from-source.txt header carries provenance pointer
    to FBE.4 + the v0.2 PyPI gate so future readers see why
    the file exists and when it becomes optional.
  - Partition-manifest admission is a 2-line addition with a
    14-line provenance block cross-referencing the FBE.4 sub-
    plan + parent plan + the empirical halt anchor. Mirrors
    FBE.3's manifest-edit comment style.
  - docs/install-from-source.md treats the README's `loam init`
    flow as the headline path; the install doc is "the
    precondition" and references the README to continue.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §9):

  - pyproject.toml edits to workspace-bootstrap, dev-sdlc,
    loam-init (Surface #2 + dispatcher fence ruling).
  - v0.2 PyPI publish (Surface #3 — captured to FUTURE_IDEAS).
  - Synth pipeline path-rewrite (parent Decision D — FBE.2b).
  - README.md / getting-started.md edits (FBE.5).

